# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Kamron C. Fazel et al. (2026). Development of Machine-Learned Interatomic Potentials to Predict Structure, Transport, and Reactivity in Platinum-Based Fuel Cells.
#   ACS Omega. doi:10.1021/acsomega.6c01745  arXiv:2505.01963v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2505.01963v2 (sha256 13cddcaa13105845...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 653 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/fazel2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the MACE committee models of the three active-learning
# stages (initial, iteration 1, iteration 2) trained on r2SCAN AIMD data
# of water, Nafion fragments, a Nafion chain and Pt(111)-Nafion-water,
# with committee-averaged validation RMSEs (Table II) and test RMSEs on a
# common test set (Table S4). Structure, proton transport and reaction
# barriers are property results.

